('palm-energy-generator-plasma-ejector', 'Palm Energy Generator: Plasma Ejector', 'rifts', 'cybernetics', NULL, 45000, '45,000 credits.', '4D6 M.D. one palm; 1D4x10 M.D. both', 1, '200 ft (61 m)', 'battery 20 blasts', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'One of the Palm Energy Generators, each sold separately; a palm fires single or both together. Battery shots as listed, unlimited on an internal energy supply. A bionic system: only for partial or full conversion cyborgs (printed 111).', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.112'),
('palm-energy-generator-stun-blaster', 'Palm Energy Generator: Stun Blaster', 'rifts', 'cybernetics', NULL, 42000, '42,000 credits.', '6D6 S.D.C. one palm; 1D6x10 S.D.C. both', 0, '500 ft (152 m)', 'battery 50 blasts', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'One of the Palm Energy Generators, each sold separately; a palm fires single or both together. Battery shots as listed, unlimited on an internal energy supply. A bionic system: only for partial or full conversion cyborgs (printed 111). The stun works as the AT-23 police stun rifle''s.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.112'),
('environmental-upgrade', 'Environmental Upgrade', 'rifts', 'cybernetics', NULL, 68000, '68,000 credits.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Seals a cyborg against leaks and toxins, with radiation shielding and temperature control, and adds 25 M.D.C. to the main body and 10 to each limb. A bionic system: only for partial or full conversion cyborgs (printed 111).', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.112'),
('aerial-jet-thrusters', 'Aerial Jet Thrusters', 'rifts', 'cybernetics', NULL, 65000, '65,000 credits.', NULL, 0, '120 miles (192 km) liquid fuel; nuclear unlimited', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Full conversion cyborgs only: 120 mph, 120 miles on liquid fuel or unlimited on nuclear (cooling after 800 miles); needs the pilot jet pack skill. A bionic system: only for partial or full conversion cyborgs (printed 111).', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.112'),
('h-u-d-visor-bionic', 'H.U.D. Visor (Bionic)', 'rifts', 'cybernetics', NULL, 95000, '95,000 credits.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A removable visor with a multi-optics camera showing radar, compass, time, depth, oxygen, floor plans and maps; combines with the SNARLS system. A bionic system: only for partial or full conversion cyborgs (printed 111).', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.112'),
('internal-iv-feed', 'Internal IV Feed', 'rifts', 'cybernetics', NULL, 5000, '5,000 credits.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Three days of nutrients, stretched to 7-10 days (double for ''borgs) with hunger pains. Most recipients are full conversion cyborgs or special forces troopers.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.112'),
('rebreather-lung', 'Rebreather Lung', 'rifts', 'cybernetics', NULL, 210000, '210,000 credits a lung.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Two hours without breathing on stored oxygen and 12 hours recycling; two lungs give 24 hours.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.112'),
('security-clearance-chip-bionic-top-secret', 'Security Clearance Chip (Bionic, Top Secret)', 'rifts', 'cybernetics', NULL, NULL, 'Not sold; tens of millions of credits on the black market.', '1D4 S.D.C. within 5 ft when it detonates', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A head implant that explodes if tampered with, killing its host (1D4 S.D.C. to those within 5 ft). The Republic requires it of workers, guards, technicians, scientists and top brass in secure posts.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.112'),
('underwater-propulsion-bionic', 'Underwater Propulsion (Bionic)', 'rifts', 'cybernetics', NULL, 72000, '72,000 credits.', NULL, 0, '150 miles (240 km) battery; nuclear indefinitely', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Propulsion in the legs or lower back: 50 mph, 150 miles on battery or indefinitely on a nuclear engine. A bionic system: only for partial or full conversion cyborgs (printed 111).', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.112-113'),
('km-200-jet-pack', 'KM-200 Jet Pack', 'rifts', 'gear', 32, 54000, '54,000 credits electric or liquid fuel; 460,000 nuclear.', NULL, 0, '360 miles on liquid fuel; nuclear effectively unlimited', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 20, 'Kiramitsu Motors'' universal jet pack for any body armor and most light power armor: top speed 120 mph, 2.5 ft long. Power is a rechargeable battery (6 hours), liquid fuel (20 minutes) or nuclear (10-year life); a nuclear pack must cool every 3 hours, and each half hour beyond that carries a 01-50% chance of overheating and burning out.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.181'),
('km-250-underwater-propulsion-pack', 'KM-250 Underwater Propulsion Pack', 'rifts', 'gear', 45, 60000, '60,000 credits fuel-powered; 500,000 nuclear.', NULL, 0, '400 miles on fuel; nuclear indefinitely', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 30, 'Kiramitsu Motors'' underwater pack that clamps or magnetically links to the back of most body armor: 35 mph underwater, 30 mph on the surface, a 3-hour oxygen supply, fairly quiet, rated to 1,200 ft. Useless on land or in space.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.182'),
('at-a11-kuru-street-armor', 'AT-A11 Kuru Street Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 15, 30000, '30,000 credits; 50% more through the underworld, and rarely on the black market.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 65, 'ArmaTech armor like a black jumpsuit of Power-Spy mesh with helmet, chest plates and shoulder, elbow and knee guards; standard for Republic police and Special Forces and favored by mercenaries, assassins and thieves. Excellent mobility, -5% prowl. Ordinary citizens may not own body armor of any kind without a special permit and military authorization.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.182'),
('kuru-style-ninja-armor', 'Kuru-Style Ninja Armor (H-Brand/Ichto)', 'rifts', 'armor', 20, 35000, '35,000 to 40,000 credits.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 50, 'H-Brand and Ichto''s knock-off of the Kuru street armor, made for ninja, ninja juicers, ninja crazies and spies: 50 to 75 M.D.C. depending on styling and plating, good mobility, -10% prowl. Black, white or dark blood red.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.182'),
('at-a14-infantry-trooper-body-armor', 'AT-A14 Infantry "Trooper" Body Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 25, 38000, '38,000 credits; 48,000 on the black market; poor to fair availability.', NULL, 0, 'thermo-imaging 2,000 ft; laser distancing 1,000 ft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 95, 'ArmaTech ceramic and metal plate with Power-Spy mesh at the joints, standard for the Republic infantry and worn by pilots, SWAT, EOD and security. Good mobility, -10% prowl, -15% to acrobatics, gymnastics, swimming and similar skills. Magnetic rucksack pad, helmet sound filter, thermo-imaging, laser distancing and a +1 to strike targeting sight; sections come off for bionic limbs.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.183'),
('at-a15-marine-heavy-combat-body-armor', 'AT-A15 Marine Heavy Combat Body Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 40, 85000, '85,000 credits or more on the black market; rarely available. Exclusive to the Republic army.', NULL, 0, 'thermo-imaging and telescopic 2,000 ft; laser distancing, night vision and infrared 1,000 ft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 120, 'Heavy plate over an exoskeleton (+8 P.S., +8 Spd, +10 ft to leaps, fatigue halved) for elite troops, Marines and officers, rated to 1,000 ft underwater. Poor mobility, -35% prowl. Extra oxygen, HUD, rucksack pad, sound filter and a +1 to strike targeting sight.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.183-184'),
('ia-100-infiltrator-body-armor', 'IA-100 Infiltrator Body Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 20, 45000, '45,000 credits on the black market; fair availability. Illegal in the Republic of Japan.', '2D4 M.D. (right-arm light laser or retractable vibro-blade)', 1, 'laser 300 ft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 60, 'Ichto''s light environmental stealth armor, used secretly by some ninja clans and by spies and assassins. Excellent mobility, -8% prowl, +5% to climb. Typically knuckle claws or spikes, a spike or grappling hook launcher, adhesive hand and foot pads, a helmet camera with 8x zoom and night vision, and a hidden wrist computer (+5% to hacking and lock-cracking).', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.184'),
('ha-4-hiker-body-armor', 'HA-4 Hiker Body Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 16, 18000, '18,000 credits; good availability. Legal in the Republic if registered and permitted.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 45, 'H-Brand''s light, non-environmental armor of padded M.D. plates with helmet and gas mask, popular with farmers, merchants, guards and explorers. Good mobility, -10% prowl.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.185'),
('ha-5-hiker-body-armor', 'HA-5 Hiker Body Armor (Samurai Styling)', 'rifts', 'armor', 22, 21000, '21,000 credits.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 45, 'The HA-4 styled like traditional splint or bamboo samurai armor, and very popular; otherwise the same armor.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.185'),
('ia-130-sumo-body-armor', 'IA-130 "Sumo" Body Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 80, 40000, '40,000 credits; scarce. Illegal in the Republic of Japan.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 145, 'Ichto''s bulky, pot-bellied environmental suit over a light exoskeleton: +6 P.S., +1 to roll with impact, but -60% prowl and to physical skills, speed cut by 20%, and twice as long to suit up. Considered a failed experiment.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.185'),
('ha-6-frontiersman-body-armor', 'HA-6 Frontiersman Body Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 24, 27000, '27,000 credits; good availability. Illegal in the Republic of Japan.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 70, 'H-Brand''s bare-bones environmental armor with the standard features, respectable mobility and good protection, sold to colonists in The Zone, adventurers and mercenaries.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.186'),
('ha-7-frontiersman-body-armor', 'HA-7 Frontiersman Body Armor (Samurai Styling)', 'rifts', 'armor', 24, 30000, '30,000 credits.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 70, 'The HA-6 made to look like traditional samurai armor; otherwise the same.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.186'),
('ha-20-juicer-environmental-armor', 'HA-20 Juicer Environmental Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 20, 38000, '38,000 credits on the black market; fair to good availability. Illegal in the Republic of Japan.', NULL, 0, 'thermo-imaging and telescopic 2,000 ft; laser distancing and targeting 1,000 ft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 75, 'Enclosed environmental armor favored by Japan''s Juicers, with samurai touches, a skull or demon helmet and often spikes. Good mobility, -10% prowl. Sound filter, thermo-imaging, telescopics, laser distancing, a +1 to strike targeting sight, HUD and passive night vision.', 'Rifts World Book 8: Japan p.186');

